From: Antonio Lopardo <antonio.lopardo@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:28:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Math environment: reasoning_gym verifier for Reasoning Gym
 tasks

verifier_type: reasoning_gym scores each answer with the scorer of its Reasoning
Gym task. The row's ground truth is a JSON object with the task name and the entry
the scorer reads (question, answer, metadata). The graded frame is reduced to the
last <answer>...</answer>, else the last \boxed{} with balanced braces, else the
whole text. The reward is binary: 1 when the scorer gives 1, else 0, because many
scorers pay small amounts for any well-formed answer. Scorers that eval() or
parse_expr the answer are refused, coin_flip is refused (its prefix credit gives "0"
full marks), complex_arithmetic and number_sorting refuse nan and inf (their
tolerance checks pass NaN), and each call has a 5 s timeout that a scorer's own
`except Exception` cannot swallow. reasoning_gym is imported in the worker, so only
runs that use it need the package. The env name reasoning_gym maps to MathEnvironment.
---
 nemo_rl/environments/math_environment.py      |   2 +
 .../environments/reasoning_gym_verifier.py    | 162 ++++++++++++++++++
 nemo_rl/environments/utils.py                 |   3 +
 3 files changed, 167 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 nemo_rl/environments/reasoning_gym_verifier.py

